 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "records are strings \"<timestamp>,task,<taskId>,<taskName>\" (root task) or \"<timestamp>,subtask,<parentId>,<taskId>,<taskName>\". The timestamp is opaque and ignored. Display the forest depth-first in pre-order: roots in record order, the children of each task in record order (a child may be recorded before its parent). Each displayed line is two spaces per depth level followed by the task name. Level 1: every record is well formed, task ids are unique and every parent exists, so the records form a forest.",
